                <head>Policy of the United States regarding problems affecting the international
                    status of Syria and Lebanon<anchor n="1" xml:id="ch38-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p>Opposition by the United States to the claim by France for a position of special
                    privilege in Syria and Lebanon; Bombardment of Damascus by French troops and
                    intervention by British forces; Criticisms by the Department of State of certain
                    provisions of the draft Anglo-French accords and of the accords as signed at
                    London on December 13, 1945</p>

































































































































































































